{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791580961,"nonce":"7F2VWEqINwqhQNq7BXWw9wH9Vs4=","message":"Cause found; fixed in d65c292. CI green.\n\n**Cause: occlusion by other windows, not a missed wake.** Reproduced on macOS (2026-10-09, Node 24.2.0): a test window covered by another window (here a second, always-on-top window of ours) receives Occluded(true); the host then holds requested frames, as it should, since nothing on screen would change. After the cover closed, Occluded(false) arrived about 2.2 s later in one run and within 1 s in another, and the held frame was drawn about 100 ms after it. A desktop with the user's windows over the test windows produces the same. The idle test's \"periodic poll\" failures are the same thing seen from the other side: focus and occlusion events from the system wake the pump during the quiet interval (4 polls is two event-driven pumps), and an Occluded event also requests a frame.\n\nChecked and ruled out: the idle sleep missing a wake (a surface acquire failure leaves the frame dirty and the non-urgent schedule retries on a 16 ms timer while the window is presentable); App Nap (a visible, frontmost-level window is not napped, and the waits that failed were for a window the system reported occluded or about to be).\n\n**Fix**\n- NativeWindowHost exposes presentable (visible, not minimized, not suspended, not occluded) and framePending.\n- Test windows open with WindowLevel.AlwaysOnTop, so the user's windows don't cover them.\n- tests/window-wait.mjs: waits count only time the window could present (budget 5 s, cap 60 s overall) and fail with the window's state (frames, framePending, presentable, visible, minimized, focused, presentable and total time).\n- native-idle counts empty wakes (a pump whose first poll finds nothing) instead of every poll, and only requires no redraw when no frame-requesting event (Occluded, Resized, ScaleFactorChanged, RedrawRequested) arrived.\n- A check with a covering window: a frame wait with a 1 s budget passed after 2.5 s covered, because covered time is not counted.\n\nFour full npm run test:native runs and the four window tests individually all passed after the change. Leaving this open for a few days of runs before closing.","files":null}]}